        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Amer, William Shakespeare\n- Works: The Tempest, Arrow in the Air\n- Places: Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire\n- Topics: acting careers, stage and screen roles\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote The Tempest, which is generally believed to have been written in 1610–11 and is often considered the last play he wrote alone.\n- Nicholas Amer was born Thomas Harold Amer on 29 September 1923 in Tranmere, Birkenhead, Cheshire.\n- Nicholas Amer was an English stage, film, and television actor known for performing in William Shakespeare's plays.\n- Nicholas Amer made his professional debut in 1948 as Ferdinand in The Tempest.\n- Nicholas Amer starred in Arrow in the Air.",
